From c55e11c92c5e1639a169983c3b487868e04e91a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:57:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: remove the dead stun test from the HURT blow danger

In borg_danger_physical() the HURT blow case sets z to d_dice * d_side
and on the next line tests z > d_dice * d_side for a +200 "stun"
penalty.  Neither value changes in between, so the test is never true
and the +200 is never added.  The case it was meant for, blows with very
few sides and many dice that tend to knock out (10d2 kicks), is already
covered by the following d_side < 3 && d_dice > 5 test, which adds 400
and is kept.

Remove the dead test.  No behaviour change.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#62.

(cherry picked from commit f1aca2e9a3d4e6ffe7e301c9aa750173dd3883bd)
---
 src/borg/borg-danger.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-danger.c b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
index f3b02d754..2bdfdba9b 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-danger.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-danger.c
@@ -110,10 +110,6 @@ static int borg_danger_physical(int i, bool full_damage)
         switch (borg_mon_blow_effect(effect->name)) {
         case MONBLOW_HURT:
             z = (d_dice * d_side);
-            /* stun */
-            if ((d_side < 3) && (z > d_dice * d_side)) {
-                n += 200;
-            }
             /* fudge- some baddies kick and they tend to KO.  Avoid close */
             /* combat like the plague.  10d2 is common but take any very low */
             /* sides and high dice count as dangerous */
-- 
